======================================================================
TOOL 4: FIBONACCI (ZECKENDORF) CODING
======================================================================

Theory: Every positive integer = unique sum of non-consecutive
Fibonacci numbers (Zeckendorf's theorem, 1972).

Reference Fibonacci sequence:
  F_1=1, F_2=2, F_3=3, F_4=5, F_5=8, F_6=13, F_7=21,
  F_8=34, F_9=55, F_10=89, F_11=144, F_12=233, F_13=377,
  F_14=610, F_15=987, F_16=1597, F_17=2584, F_18=4181, F_19=6765

Zeckendorf representations of important numbers:
       n |              Indices |                  Fibonacci sum |            Bitstring
  -------+----------------------+--------------------------------+---------------------
       7 |               [2, 4] |                          2 + 5 |                 1010
      21 |                  [7] |                             21 |              1000000
      42 |               [5, 8] |                         8 + 34 |             10010000
     168 |           [3, 7, 11] |                   3 + 21 + 144 |          10001000100
    6174 | [1, 4, 6, 13, 16, 18] | 1 + 5 + 13 + 377 + 1597 + 4181 |   101001000000101001

Verification -- no consecutive Fibonacci indices used:
  7: indices [2, 4] -- consecutive? False
  21: indices [7] -- consecutive? False
  42: indices [5, 8] -- consecutive? False
  168: indices [3, 7, 11] -- consecutive? False
  6174: indices [1, 4, 6, 13, 16, 18] -- consecutive? False

Pattern analysis:
  7 = 5 + 2          -- uses F_4 + F_2 (even indices)
  21 = 21            -- IS a Fibonacci number (F_7)
  42 = 34 + 8        -- uses F_8 + F_5
  168 = 144 + 21 + 3 -- uses F_11 + F_7 + F_3 (all odd indices!)
  6174 = 4181+1597+377+13+5+1 -- 6 terms

Zeckendorf statistics for 1..1000:
  1 terms: 15 numbers (1.5%)
  2 terms: 84 numbers (8.4%)
  3 terms: 226 numbers (22.6%)
  4 terms: 331 numbers (33.1%)
  5 terms: 252 numbers (25.2%)
  6 terms: 84 numbers (8.4%)
  7 terms: 8 numbers (0.8%)
  Average terms: 4.005
  (Theory predicts ~log_phi(n) / (1+1/phi) terms on average)

  Numbers that are Fibonacci numbers: [21]


