TOOL 5: FIBONACCI HASH
======================================================================

hash_F(n) = F_n mod M. Testing collision properties.

M = 97, hashing keys 0..999:
  Fib hash:    69 distinct values, max bucket 22, 69 buckets with collision, 931 total collisions
  Simple mod:  97 distinct values, max bucket 11
  Pisano period pi(97) = 196
  Fib hash cycles every 196 keys => 196 distinct outputs max

M = 127, hashing keys 0..999:
  Fib hash:    97 distinct values, max bucket 16, 97 buckets with collision, 903 total collisions
  Simple mod:  127 distinct values, max bucket 8
  Pisano period pi(127) = 256
  Fib hash cycles every 256 keys => 256 distinct outputs max

M = 251, hashing keys 0..999:
  Fib hash:    157 distinct values, max bucket 12, 157 buckets with collision, 843 total collisions
  Simple mod:  251 distinct values, max bucket 4
  Pisano period pi(251) = 250
  Fib hash cycles every 250 keys => 250 distinct outputs max

M = 1009, hashing keys 0..999:
  Fib hash:    92 distinct values, max bucket 24, 92 buckets with collision, 908 total collisions
  Simple mod:  1000 distinct values, max bucket 1
  Pisano period pi(1009) = 126
  Fib hash cycles every 126 keys => 126 distinct outputs max

M = 4096, hashing keys 0..999:
  Fib hash:    897 distinct values, max bucket 2, 103 buckets with collision, 103 total collisions
  Simple mod:  1000 distinct values, max bucket 1
  Pisano period pi(4096) = 6144
  Fib hash cycles every 6144 keys => 6144 distinct outputs max

Application: Fibonacci hash for tournament vertex labeling
  For n-vertex tournament, label vertices 0..n-1.
  Use F-hash to map vertex pairs to edge buckets.

  n=5: 10 edges, 5 distinct F-hashes (mod 10), coverage 50.0%
  n=7: 21 edges, 7 distinct F-hashes (mod 21), coverage 33.3%
  n=11: 55 edges, 12 distinct F-hashes (mod 55), coverage 21.8%
  n=13: 78 edges, 44 distinct F-hashes (mod 78), coverage 56.4%


