TOOL 7: FIBONACCI-WEIGHTED PRIME COUNTER
======================================================================

pi_F(N) = sum_{p <= N, p prime} F_{index(p)}
where index(p) = position of p in the prime sequence (1-indexed).

       N |  pi(N) |              pi_F(N) |      pi_F/pi |  log(pi_F)
  -------+--------+----------------------+--------------+-----------
      10 |      4 |                    7 |         1.75 |     1.9459
      20 |      8 |                   54 |         6.75 |     3.9890
      50 |     15 |                 1596 |       106.40 |     7.3753
     100 |     25 |               196417 |      7856.68 |    12.1880
     200 |     46 |           4807526975 | 104511455.98 |    22.2934
     500 |     95 | 83621143489848422976 | 880222563051036032.00 |    45.8728
    1000 |    168 | 150804340016807970735635273952047184 | 897644881052428463807720010547200.00 |    81.0013
    2000 |    303 | 2464593359921179141398048006246675396881836888835835456250887804 | 8133971484888379359060952520471285151681586828897221561286656.00 |   145.9649
    5000 |    669 | 76071434434275996245450651810502251293053343675909383072806500450427721205029553200424258508447999692160174311581845255665234840742378430528 | 113709169557961124356016994470955876173001896477968220667328631427693703541743311607341667522713955479227485402291132961782556193663746048.00 |   322.0884
   10000 |   1229 | 82091869400456868675788383971950136567814826817182809854548600805886244668090124354145430988935852086652783963270701783629331573637990153274350120161320558698187639465895520505298827854557494025169000487710175614104306232651487891685603022411399062367507068 | 66795662652934802107880941574331756103496333396949449829719077926999699622152238055074242780290483818076239211863167858354718834414427070583480050177376049077082034250634045816743415246093305251484598138412713082375209004583542063627217168920691353845760.00 |   591.5670

Growth analysis:
  pi(N) ~ N/ln(N)  (prime number theorem)
  F_k ~ phi^k / sqrt(5)
  pi_F(N) ~ sum_{k=1}^{pi(N)} phi^k/sqrt(5)
         ~ phi^{pi(N)+1} / (sqrt(5)*(phi-1))
         ~ phi^{N/ln(N)} / sqrt(5)

  So log(pi_F(N)) ~ (N/ln(N)) * ln(phi)
  ln(phi) = 0.481212

